2. CONTENT PACK GRANT

   Ballistic API exists to load third-party content. Nothing in Section 1 is
   intended to restrict that, and this section grants the rights needed to do
   it.

   "Content Pack" means a collection of data and assets (JSON definitions,
   models, textures, sounds, animations, scripts, and similar files) that is
   loaded at runtime by Ballistic API and does not include any part of the
   Software's code or assets.

   You are granted a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable right to:

   (a) Create Content Packs for Ballistic API, for any purpose, including
       commercial purposes.

   (b) Distribute, sell, and license your Content Packs on any terms you
       choose, through any channel.

   (c) Use Ballistic API's pack formats, JSON schemas, field names, directory
       layouts, registry identifiers, and documented public API for the purpose
       of authoring, loading, or interoperating with Content Packs.

   (d) Write separate mods, tools, editors, validators, or libraries that
       interoperate with Ballistic API through its public API or pack formats.

   You own your Content Pack. This license claims no ownership over, and
   imposes no licensing terms on, content you create. Loading your work through
   Ballistic API does not make it a derivative work of the Software, and no
   attribution to Ballistic API is required.

   This grant is irrevocable: it cannot be withdrawn from Content Packs already
   published, and it survives any future change to this license.


3. LIMITS OF THE GRANT

   Section 2 does not permit you to:

   (a) Redistribute the Software's own code, binaries, or bundled assets,
       whether modified or unmodified, except as allowed in Section 4.

   (b) Present a Content Pack in a way that implies it is Ballistic API itself,
       or that it is endorsed by or affiliated with the project.


4. MODPACK INCLUSION

   You may include Ballistic API in a modpack, free or paid, provided that all
   of the following hold:

   (a) The modpack uses a distribution format that fetches Ballistic API from
       an official distribution page operated or authorised by the copyright
       holder. The end user's launcher performs the download; the modpack
       itself carries a reference, not the file. CurseForge manifests and
       Modrinth .mrpack index entries are the intended examples.

   (b) The modpack does not bundle, mirror, re-host, or otherwise include a
       copy of the Ballistic API JAR.

   (c) Ballistic API is distributed unmodified. You may not patch, repackage,
       strip, recompile, or alter the JAR in any way.

   (d) Configuration files and Content Packs shipped alongside are unaffected
       by this section and remain governed by Section 2.

   This permission is automatically revoked for any modpack that breaches (a)
   through (c).


